From 83b6ff9e861dd6a8d1143776b36a9fb83dd0be45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:52:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: EIC model, PORT routing to peripheral function A

mchp-eic (U2254, PIC32CM MC00 and JH01): edge and level detection on the
16 EXTINT inputs and NMI, W1C flags with level re-assertion, the EIC
interrupt, event outputs, NMI to the CPU even with the EIC disabled.
Synchronous edges need the EIC clock (GCLK_EIC, or CLK_ULP32K with
CKSEL); asynchronous ones and levels do not. A change of CTRLA.ENABLE
while the configuration needs the clock and the clock is off stalls
SYNCBUSY.ENABLE until it runs; checked on PIC32CM MC00 silicon with a
test image whose transcript matches the twin byte for byte.

mchp-port gains "func-a" outputs: the pad level of pins muxed to
function A; the SoC wires them to the EIC from the pad signal table
(OR-ed where several pins share an input). MchpDeviceInfo carries the
signal table. New overlay-driven PMUX write hook. New qtest
pic32cm-eic-test.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
